- type: url
  value: https://github.com/epinowcast/epidist/
abstract: Understanding and accurately estimating epidemiological delay distributions
  is important for public health policy. These estimates influence epidemic situational
  awareness, control strategies, and resource allocation. This package provides methods
  to address the key challenges in estimating these distributions, including truncation,
  interval censoring, and dynamical biases. These issues are frequently overlooked,
  resulting in biased conclusions. Built on top of 'brms', it allows for flexible
  modelling including time-varying spatial components and partially pooled estimates
  of demographic characteristics.
